      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T14:00:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible that, while the caller of `pkvm_pgtable_lookup()` is playing with the PTE pointer, the corresponding page table page of this PTE pointer may be recycled by another page table API? The page table API usually holds a mmu lock while playing with the PTE pointer. Now returning the PTE pointer to the caller indicates there is no mmu lock protection?",
      "revId": "2bea620f7493604b0acb28dfdd2e0333fdf6fc34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
