      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T11:12:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I cannot recall there is a specific reason we have to use pointer in the pgtable callbacks. Maybe can refactor callbacks to accept the raw value rather than pointer, e.g., pte_present/pte_annotated, while keeping the pte_set/pte_get to take pointer, so that no need to return the PTE pointer but a raw pte value, which is more safe?",
      "parentUuid": "3a562d25_d27e3a1c",
      "revId": "2bea620f7493604b0acb28dfdd2e0333fdf6fc34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
